To evaluate the Cholesky and the LU decompositions in \POSITA{}, we execute \Rpotrf{} and \Rgetrf{} using RTX3090, RTX4090, RX7900, and Agilex FPGA.
Both \Rpotrf{} and \Rgetrf{} call \Rgemm{} for updating the trailing matrix. 
We run the two decomposition routines on an $N \times N$ matrix. 
Since \Rpotrf{} factorizes a Hermitian and positive definite matrix, we initialize a matrix $X$ with the normal distribution and compute a matrix $A = X^{T}X$ as the input matrix.
By measuring the execution time of the two routines, we compute the performance with the number of operations as $\frac{N^3}{3}$ and $\frac{2 N^3}{3}$ for \Rpotrf{} and \Rgetrf{}, respectively. 
