\model consists of two steps: \one \emph{Knowledge Acquisition}, which extracts predicted labels and corresponding rationales from teacher MLLMs; and \two \emph{Multi-Teacher Knowledge Distillation}, which LoRA fine-tunes the student MLLM on the acquired teacher knowledge. Specifically, the second step encompasses two stages: \emph{Global Knowledge Learning} and \emph{Complementary Knowledge Fusion}. Stage 1 equips the student model with reasonable logic to detect out-of-context news, while Stage 2 reinforces the student's capability on ``hard cases'' and refines its discernment. 
