Lastly, we observe that removing LoRA fine-tuning from Step 2 results in inferior performance compared to not introducing Step 2. We conjecture that applying DPO in isolation may confuse the student model regarding generation targets. However, with proper guidance (LoRA fine-tuning), DPO can realize its full potential and benefit learning on more difficult examples.

