\section{Procedural Articulated Asset Generators}
\label{sec:examples}

Using our custom joint and utility nodes, users can create a variety of physically accurate, kinematically diverse, photorealistic assets. We demonstrate the capabilities of Infinigen-Sim by developing procedural generators for five categories of articulated assets including doors, toasters, fridges, dishwashers, and lamps. These articulated procedural generators were created in 1-7 hours per object class by novice and intermediate Blender users, mostly dominated by time to create the static procedural asset.

Examples of assets sampled from these generators can be seen in Fig. \ref{fig:asset_examples}. Table \ref{tab:combinations} showcases the variations we consider for each asset category. Similar assets in PartNet-Mobility \citep{Xiang_2020_SAPIEN} are quite limited in quantity.

\begin{figure}[t]
    \centering
    \includegraphics[width=\textwidth]{figures/custom_dists.pdf}
    \caption{Comparison of asset parameter distributions. The top row shows the default distribution used for handle length and handle-to-hinge distance. The bottom row shows an expanded distribution where these parameters are varied over a wider range.}
    \label{fig:custom_dists}
