\section{Introduction}
Large Language Models (LLMs) like GPT-4 \cite{achiam2023gpt} and Llama-3 \cite{dubey2024llama} have found widespread use in various domains, including finance \cite{zhao2024optimizing}, tourism \cite{meyer2024comparisonllmfinetuningmethods}, healthcare \cite{mishra-etal-2023-pal}, education \cite{lee-etal-2023-peep}, and customer support \cite{obadinma-etal-2022-bringing}. While LLMs have been applied to legal tasks such as judgment prediction, summarization, and case retrieval \cite{joshi-etal-2024-il,feng-etal-2024-legal}, there's a notable gap in their application to consumer law, especially for assisting individuals with everyday grievances. This is particularly crucial in India.

