Fig. \ref{Fig: SR scheme comparision} depicts the ergodic SR performance of conventional RSMA schemes, CS-RSMA and SDMA. It can be observed that RSMA schemes, including CS-RSMA, bring benefits in the medium SNR regime compared to SDMA. Furthermore, CS-RSMA slightly outperforms conventional RSMA schemes. The ergodic SR led by different transmission modes under CS-RSMA is depicted in Fig. \ref{Fig: SR mode comparision}, together with the performance of CS-RSMA given by adaptive alphabet/mode selection as a reference. It can be observed that the transmission modes that enable the common stream achieve higher SR than Mode 1, i.e., SDMA, at medium SNR. At high SNR, Mode 1 dominates as other modes saturate at lower SR, as suggested by Remark \ref{Remark: upper bound on SR}.

