% In this paper we investigate how the concept of network tomography could be
% achieved with cortical neuronal circuits for both morphological, topological and electrical classification of neurons. We firstly designed two open-access autonomous simulation support of various neuronal circuits from the Blue Brain Project realistic models, named Neurpy and Neurgen. We extract the simulated data to develop a classifying model to infer internal network characteristics based on the measured endpoint data. We investigate the use of information theory in cell-to-cell links. 
% We also separately train many different classifiers to identify
% the specific cell type (and sub-group types) from input-output voltage measurements, achieving accuracies of up to 70\% while comparing the performance between the individual classification algorithms.
