 as ${N_{RF}}$ increases, the performance gap between the FP-PMO algorithm and FD-OPT becomes smaller. When the number of RF chains ${N_{RF}}$ is equal to ${N_t}$, the performance of the proposed algorithm is essentially the same as that of the FD-OPT algorithm. This is due to the physical structure. 

