\section{Conclusion}

The research presented in this paper introduces a novel RAG-based agentic model for content-aware layout generation, representing a significant advancement in the field. By integrating a RAG database with a collaborative multi-agent system comprising a layout generator, a VLM grader, and a VLM feedback agent, the proposed approach addresses the limitations of existing methods and leverages the strengths of retrieval-augmented generation and autonomous agentic frameworks. The model's performance, evaluated on the challenging PKU PosterLayout dataset using a comprehensive set of graphic and content-aware metrics, demonstrates the potential of this integrated approach for producing high-quality, content-aware layouts. This work not only contributes to the field of automated graphic design but also highlights the increasing capabilities of LLMs and VLMs for tackling complex creative tasks through sophisticated system design and the incorporation of iterative refinement processes. Future research could explore the scalability and generalizability of this model to other design domains and investigate more advanced techniques for agent collaboration and feedback.

